Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

THE LAST SURFACE THAT ASSUMED A VISITOR'S COUNTRY

GEO-004 set the rule the rest of this site holds: a New York surface shows no
Canadian figure and an Ontario surface shows no United States one. verify-geo
enforces it on every page that NAMES a market.

The studio names none. So the rule never reached it — while the header and the
footer link it from all 26 New York markets, and every figure it printed was
Canadian:

  catalog.ts              bandForWork(work), left at its 'CA' default
  FloorStudio.tsx         Intl.NumberFormat('en-CA', { currency: 'CAD' })
  the budget field        labelled "optional, CAD"
  floor-studio/page.tsx   told machines the range was "in Canadian dollars"
  studioLeadNote          wrote CAD into the estimating desk's own note

A homeowner in Amherst read a United States band on /service-areas/amherst,
tapped "see it in your room", and was quoted in Canadian dollars. That is two
published versions of one fact, which is the single class of error this
repository exists to prevent.

ASKED FOR AND CARRIED, NEVER INFERRED

StudioDesign carries a country. No IP lookup and no locale sniffing: a visitor
on a Toronto laptop planning a Buffalo rental is not a Canadian job, and
guessing would put the wrong currency in front of them with no way to see why.

  · THE CITY PAGES SET IT. All 89 carry a studio CTA linking ?region=US or
    ?region=CA. Until now they reached the studio only through the global
    chrome, which is exactly how the defect survived a currency patch.
  · THE STUDIO STATES IT. A region control above the range says which bands are
    in use and where they apply, linked to /pricing where both are published.
  · THE SHARE CODE CARRIES IT. n=US only when it is not the home country, so no
    Ontario link that already exists changed meaning or grew by a byte.
  · THE HANDOFF CARRIES IT. estimateHref adds region, so the fixed price is
    written against the band the visitor was actually shown — the same defect
    one step further down the funnel, closed in the same patch.

GEO-005 HAD ALREADY DONE THE HARD HALF

EstimateResult has carried `currency` from the band it was given since then, so
nothing downstream had to learn a country — only to read the currency instead of
assuming one. Both figure sets are their own published band times the area. NO
EXCHANGE RATE IS APPLIED ANYWHERE, because nobody published one.

NAMING DEBT, RECORDED RATHER THAN HIDDEN

The fields are still estimatedLowCad, estimatedHighCad, perSqftCad, budgetCad.
The VALUES are right — whatever band came in, with `currency` saying which — but
the names now say CAD about a figure that may be USD. Renaming crosses
packages/shared, the chat tool, the estimate API and the lead schema: a patch of
its own, not one to bury inside this one. It is a misleading name and not a
misleading claim — nothing a visitor or a machine reads says CAD about a USD
figure. It is in the log so it is not found as a surprise.

Verified: 66 guards pass, verify:geo and the green gate included. 34 new
assertions in region.test.ts, holding the rule the studio had escaped: a New
York design never carries a Canadian figure, an omitted country still means
Ontario, a share link opens in the currency it was built in, and an Ontario link
gains no parameter. 65,490 across the floor-studio, navigation and assistant
suites, 0 failed.

docs/AUDIT_03_INTEGRATION.md moves from A− to A. The contradiction that held the
grade is gone; what is left is the naming debt above, GC-021, GC-023, and
ecowoodshardwood.com, which needs a DNS panel rather than a commit.

